<%= render "shared/navbar" %>

<%# Standalone, publicly reachable trending page (nav link) — also the source the
    feed's lazy `turbo_frame_tag "trending"` sidebar extracts by matching id.

    Two renderings of the SAME `Hujah.trending` set share this one action/template
    (Phase 2.5): a direct/full-page hit renders the rich, ranked cards; the feed
    sidebar's lazy frame request renders the original minimal list unchanged.
    `turbo_frame_request?` (turbo-rails) is the load-bearing signal — Turbo tags a
    frame's own fetch with a `Turbo-Frame: <id>` request header, which is exactly how
    the sidebar's `turbo_frame_tag "trending", src: trending_path, loading: :lazy`
    asks for this page. No second query: both branches render the same @hujahs. %>
<main class="max-w-xl mx-auto px-4 py-6">
  <%= turbo_frame_tag "trending" do %>
    <% if turbo_frame_request? %>
      <%= render "trending", hujahs: @hujahs %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render "trending_rich", hujahs: @hujahs %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</main>
